# name: ADB state
# description: Masks a live adbd. Runs at boot-completed, because init has not written these props yet at the service stage. Turn it off if you rely on tooling that reads adb state props.
# enabled: 1
# stage: boot-completed

# Why '# stage: boot-completed':
#   init writes init.svc.* and service.adb.* as those services start, so
#   at the service stage they either do not exist yet or are about to be
#   overwritten. 'reset' never creates a prop, so these rules would be
#   silent no-ops there. This is the one group in the fork's prop set
#   that genuinely needs the later stage.
#
# Scope, so nobody is surprised:
#   Nothing here stops adbd. These are prop spoofs only, and none of
#   them persist past a reboot. A running adbd keeps working and an
#   active ADB session is not dropped.
#
#   What can notice: tooling that reads adb state from these props
#   rather than asking adbd. If you develop against this device and
#   something starts reporting ADB as unavailable, this preset is the
#   first thing to turn off.
reset   init.svc.adbd            stopped
clear   init.svc_debug_pid.adbd
delete  service.adb.root
delete  service.adb.tcp.port
